<title>GERMANY: Pan-German April industry orders rise 3.3 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German April industry orders rise 3.3 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS  Apr 97     Mar 97     Apr 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	  +3.3	 +0.9	 +2.6</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +6.2	 +5.5	 +0.7</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     103.0	 99.7	 97.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data. @</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following month-on-month details:</p>
<p>				     Apr 97     Mar 97   Apr 97 index</p>
<p> Total domestic orders	  +3.1	 +0.6	  92.9</p>
<p> Total foreign orders	   +3.6	 +1.3	 123.2</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	     +1.6	 +1.1	 104.9</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +2.1	 +1.2	  97.1</p>
<p>	     foreign		+0.8	 +1.2	 122.9</p>
<p> Capital goods		    +3.9	 +1.1	 104.1</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +3.3	 +0.6	  91.1</p>
<p>	     foreign		+5.0	 +1.4	 125.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables     +6.5	 unch	  96.1</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +6.2	 -1.1	  85.4</p>
<p>	     foreign		+7.0	 +1.8	 118.6</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Mar/Apr 97 with Jan/Feb 97:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +2.5</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +3.0</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +2.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +3.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +1.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +3.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Mar/Apr 97 with Mar/Apr 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +5.4</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +1.5</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +11.6</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +8.9</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +1.9</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +3.0</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
